# Install

If you have Rust, one command does it:

```sh
cargo install hql
```

Then check that it runs:

```sh
hql eval '40 + 2'
```

```text
42
```

That's all you need. Start with [Hello world](/draft/book/01-hello-world/),
the first chapter of the book.

## No Rust yet?

Get it from [rustup.rs](https://rustup.rs). HQL needs Rust 1.95 or newer.
If you'd rather not install Rust at all, download a ready-made binary instead.

## Ready-made binaries

Every [release](https://github.com/ewiger/hql/releases) has a binary for
Linux, for macOS and for Windows. Download the archive for your machine,
unpack it, and move `hql` somewhere on your `PATH`:

=== "macOS, Apple silicon"

    ```sh
    tar -xzf hql-*-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz
    sudo mv hql-*-aarch64-apple-darwin/hql /usr/local/bin/
    ```

=== "macOS, Intel"

    ```sh
    tar -xzf hql-*-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz
    sudo mv hql-*-x86_64-apple-darwin/hql /usr/local/bin/
    ```

=== "Linux, x86_64"

    ```sh
    tar -xzf hql-*-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz
    sudo mv hql-*-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/hql /usr/local/bin/
    ```

=== "Windows, x86_64"

    ```powershell
    tar -xzf (Get-Item hql-*-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.tar.gz)
    ```

    Then move `hql.exe` from the unpacked folder to a folder on your `PATH`.

Each archive has a `.sha256` file next to it. To check the download, run
this before you unpack it:

```sh
shasum -a 256 -c hql-*.tar.gz.sha256    # on Linux: sha256sum -c
```

On Windows, `Get-FileHash` prints the digest to compare with the one in the
file:

```powershell
Get-FileHash (Get-Item hql-*.tar.gz)
```

## The newest code

To try what's on `main` before it's released:

```sh
cargo install --git https://github.com/ewiger/hql
```

Or, from a clone of the repository:

```sh
cargo install --path .
```

## Update or remove

Run `cargo install hql` again to update to the newest release.
`cargo uninstall hql` removes it.

## Packages

`hql` works on its own. Packages add extra modules, such as `ml`, and
`hql package install` builds them on your machine, so they need `cargo`.
[Installing packages](/draft/book/36-installing-packages/) shows how.

!!! note "Before 1.0"

    Until HQL reaches 1.0, a minor release can break programs that worked
    before. The [changelog](https://github.com/ewiger/hql/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)
    lists every such change.
